<title>SOUTH KOREA: KIA Motors to raise exports to 800,000.</title>
<headline>KIA Motors to raise exports to 800,000.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kia Motors, one of South Korea's three largest carmakers, said on Monday it would raise exports to 800,000 units by 2001 from 321,950 in 1996.</p>
<p>Kia said in a statement its annual overseas production would increase to 520,000 units by 2001 from 69,042 in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be producing cars in 16 countries by 2001,&quot; said a Kia spokesman.</p>
<p>Those countries include Indonesia, Russia, China, India, Turkey and Brazil.</p>
